I'll start by exploring the project structure to understand how columns are defined, edited, and how tasks are created with profiles.Let me explore the board directory and find column dialogs.Let me explore the full project structure and the board-related files.Let me examine the profile selection components and the modals in detail.Let me check which board components are actually wired into the app (new board view vs. legacy Kanban.vue).I now have a complete picture. The active "tasks" app is `KanbanBoardView.vue` (which shares `SprintBoardColumn.vue`, `SprintBoardModals.vue`, and `SprintBoardView.vue`). Columns live on `board.columns` (kanban) and are materialized for sprint boards.

Here's my plan:

## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements:** Let each board column define a set of profiles that are automatically pre-selected when a task is created in that column (both kanban and sprint boards).

**Strategic Approach:**
- Add a `profiles: []` field to the column data model (kanban + sprint).
- Persist/resolve it in the kanban store (`addColumn`, `updateColumn`, `addSprintColumn`, `updateSprintColumn`, `materializeSprintColumns`, `syncColumnOrder`, getters `buildViewColumns`/`sprintColumns`, and board export/import).
- Add a profile picker to the column dialog in `SprintBoardModals.vue`.
- Pre-fill `newTask.selectedProfiles` from the destination column when opening the New Task dialog (and re-apply when the kanban column picker changes).
- Pass `profiles` through the `column-created`/`column-updated` handlers in `KanbanBoardView.vue` and `SprintBoardView.vue`.

**Dependencies & Risks:** `Object.assign` in the `updateColumn` mutation would wipe `profiles` if the key is sent as `undefined`, so I only include it when provided. Board export/import must carry the field so portability is preserved.

**Target Files:**
| File | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| `src/store/kanban.js` | Modify |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` | Modify |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | Modify |

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach
Changes are applied per file below; each is self-contained and keeps existing behaviour intact.

