## Notes

- **Why `SprintBoardColumn.vue`:** it is the shared column used by both the kanban canvas and the sprint board (the kanban view renders through `SprintBoardCanvas`), and it is the one that has the **status icon** the request refers to. `KanbanBoardColumn.vue` is the legacy column (no status icon) — say the word and I'll mirror the same avatar group there.
- **Data source:** columns store profile **names** (`column.profiles`), so the header resolves them to full profile objects from the active project (`$project.$state.profiles`, falling back to `$storex.projects.ai.profiles`). Unknown names still render an initial, so nothing breaks pre-load.
- **Avatar content (in priority order):** `profile.avatar` image → `profile.icon` (Font Awesome) → name initial. The profile `color` tints the icon/text when defined.
- **DaisyUI avatar group:** `avatar-group -space-x-2` with `ring-1 ring-base-100` separators, a `+N` overflow avatar (`+` count) when more than 4 profiles are configured, and a `tooltip tooltip-bottom` with the profile name on each avatar (accessible, not color-only).
- **No layout regressions:** the group is `shrink-0` and sits between the icon badge and the task count; the column title keeps its `flex-1 truncate`.
- **Accessibility:** every avatar has a tooltip naming the profile; the group only renders when the column actually defines profiles (empty state unchanged).

