## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements:** The column header's avatar group must display each default profile's **`avatar` image URL** (the profile's real photo), not just an initial.

**Strategic Approach:**
- Make `availableProfiles` resolve profiles from every place they are cached (`project.$state.profiles`, `$storex.projects.profiles`, `$storex.projects.ai.profiles`, `$storex.profiles.profiles`), so names resolve to real objects that include `avatar`.
- Make `columnProfiles` ensure it returns the **full** resolved object (with `avatar`) even when a name-only object was stored.
- Render the avatar via a new `profileAvatar(profile)` helper (`avatar_url || avatar`, matching `ProfileAvatar.vue`), and fall back to the initial only when there is genuinely no avatar URL or the image fails to load (`@error`).

**Dependencies & Risks:** Accessing the `$storex.profiles.profiles` getter dereferences `activeProject.project_id`, so it is guarded by an `activeProject` check. `@error` tracking avoids an infinite loop on broken URLs.

**Target File:** `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardColumn.vue` (Modify)

