## Behaviour Summary
- Each column chip in the avatar group now shows the profile's real **`avatar` image URL** (the same field the profile editor writes and `ProfileCard`/`ProfileAvatar` consume).
- Profiles without an avatar URL, or whose image fails to load, gracefully fall back to the profile initial (tinted by `profile.color` when set) — no broken-image icons.
- No layout change: the group stays `shrink-0` right after the status icon, with the `+N` overflow avatar unchanged.

## Accessibility notes
- Every avatar keeps its `tooltip tooltip-bottom` naming the profile, so the image is never the only signal.
- `alt` is set to the profile name; the initial fallback is real text content.

## Note
The active board column is `SprintBoardColumn.vue` (shared by the sprint board and the kanban canvas via `SprintBoardCanvas`), which is the one that renders the **status icon** you referred to. `KanbanBoardColumn.vue` is the legacy column (colour-dot only, no status icon) and was left untouched. If you'd like the same avatar group there too, say the word and I'll mirror it.

